readline: end a line at CR or LF; CR LF and LF CR are one line end

Purpose: readline ended a line only at LF, so a terminal's CR alone did
nothing and CR LF needed the terminal driver to translate CR.  Now CR and
LF each end a line and the second byte of a CR LF or LF CR pair is
ignored, also when the next readline() call reads it (the state is kept
per task, i.e. per shell session).  CR NUL from Telnet is one line end too
(NUL is ignored as before).
Zephyr: subsys/shell/shell.c process_nl() and state_collect(): CR, LF,
CR LF and LF CR are each one Enter.

